  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Week 25 - captured 2026-09-24 by the Gmail-lesson-intake Way (DR-0312):
  // Darrell forwarded (from dpoe@illinois.edu, his Lesson. marker) the Level Up
  // Coding issue Deployment Patterns Every Engineer Should Know (Nikki Siapno,
  // Sep 24 2026), which came through complete. Word first: deployed is not
  // released (John 2:4; Galatians 4:4 - the Son never an unproven change, the
  // parallel is timing only); built before it is brought (1 Kings 6:7);
  // switching back is not undoing (Esther 8:8); the canary is Daniel's ten days
  // (Daniel 1:12-16); the one inside the ninety and nine is measured separately
  // (Luke 15:4; Joshua 7); the fruit, not the appearance (John 7:24; Matthew
  // 7:20) with this house's own DR-0317 and DR-0125 as the worked cases; flags
  // need an owner or they become Nehushtan (Numbers 21:8; 2 Kings 18:4); and the
  // bright line - test the tool, never put the Word into a variant (Galatians
  // 1:8; Psalms 119:89). Every verse filled from the repo KJV corpus and pinned.
