    "bigIdea": "THE NEW PLAYERS - OPEN WEIGHTS, A JUST WEIGHT, AND THE ONE WHO PUTTETH DOWN ONE AND SETTETH UP ANOTHER. Darrell forwarded a Morning Brew newsletter on 2026-10-07 with one word over it, \"Lesson\": two Western companies are releasing open-weight A.I. models, which the newsletter defines plainly as models whose learned numbers you may \"download and customize them with their own proprietary data\" rather than rent across somebody else's boundary. That is a real good, and this house already stands on it - our own machines serve open-weights models today, and nobody far away can switch our copy off. But the industry has announced OPEN weights, and the Word has always required a JUST weight: \"A false balance is abomination to the LORD: but a just weight is his delight\" (Proverbs 11:1) and \"all the weights of the bag are his work\" (Proverbs 16:11). Open is ACCESS; just is TRUTH. So the week teaches the distinction the marketing collapses, and the Word already governs the question under it: who hands out a seat at the table (\"But God is the judge: he putteth down one, and setteth up another\" (Psalms 75:7)); why a trillion parameters is not a foundation (\"An horse is a vain thing for safety: neither shall he deliver any by his great strength\" (Psalms 33:17)); and the hinge - a weights file is a thing anyone may change, so it is held against the one standard no one may (\"Add thou not unto his words, lest he reprove thee, and thou be found a liar\" (Proverbs 30:6); \"For ever, O LORD, thy word is settled in heaven\" (Psalms 119:89)). Auditability is a possibility; proving is a practice. And a badge of origin proves nothing in either direction, because \"in righteousness shalt thou judge thy neighbour\" (Leviticus 19:15).",
