        "THE HINGE: anyone may change what anyone may download, so the copy you run may not be the copy published. The answer is not refusing openness; it is holding the alterable against the unalterable. \"Ye shall not add unto the word which I command you, neither shall ye diminish ought from it\" (Deuteronomy 4:2) \"Add thou not unto his words, lest he reprove thee, and thou be found a liar\" (Proverbs 30:6) \"For ever, O LORD, thy word is settled in heaven\" (Psalms 119:89) THE MODEL IS MODIFIABLE, THE WORD IS NOT - so the Word stays in the text on disk and checks the model, never the reverse.",
        "THE CEILING OF AUDITABILITY: \"Prove all things; hold fast that which is good\" (1 Thessalonians 5:21) was a command before it was a selling point, and the Bereans held gladness and examination together (\"searched the scriptures daily, whether those things were so\" (Acts 17:11)). One witness does not establish a matter (\"at the mouth of two witnesses, or at the mouth of three witnesses, shall the matter be established\" (Deuteronomy 19:15)), and a vendor speaking of its own product is an interested witness. A model that CAN be audited and never IS audited bought nothing.",
        "JUDGE THE WORK, NOT THE FACE: reported hesitancy about models of one origin is a market fact; converting it into a moral rule leaves the Word. \"thou shalt not respect the person of the poor, nor honor the person of the mighty: but in righteousness shalt thou judge thy neighbour\" (Leviticus 19:15) \"God is no respecter of persons\" (Acts 10:34) \"Judge not according to the appearance, but judge righteous judgment\" (John 7:24) Both over-reaches fall; the real risk stays - an unexamined binary from ANY source, answered by examining the thing in hand.",
        "ONE LAMP, TWO EFFECTS: \"all things that are reproved are made manifest by the light\" (Ephesians 5:13) \"he that doeth truth cometh to the light\" (John 3:21) \"He that walketh uprightly walketh surely\" (Proverbs 10:9) The asymmetry is in the builder, not the lamp - so build what can be looked at, and openness is on your side.",
        "THE READABLE BILL: difficult-to-budget is the article's own honest phrase. \"Be thou diligent to know the state of thy flocks, and look well to thy herds\" (Proverbs 27:23) - diligent to KNOW, so a surprise invoice is a flock whose state is unknown. With the restraint beside it: \"riches certainly make themselves wings; they fly away as an eagle toward heaven\" (Proverbs 23:5) and \"A prudent man foreseeth the evil, and hideth himself\" (Proverbs 22:3) - the generator in the garage, unchanged by two new vendors.",
        "WHAT WE DO: the news widens the road, it does not redirect us; the proving is the work and the acquiring is not. \"Through wisdom is an house builded; and by understanding it is established\" (Proverbs 24:3) names the Resources; \"Except the LORD build the house, they labour in vain that build it\" (Psalms 127:1) names what is not among them. And the One holding it all: \"he is before all things, and by him all things consist\" (Colossians 1:17) - Jesus, the Son of Yahweh, the Lamb (John 1:29)."
