      "theme": "\"Through faith we understand that the worlds were framed by the word of God, so that things which are seen were not made of things which do appear.\" (Hebrews 11:3) Measure and number are part of a frame the Word wrote, before anyone was there to discover them. \"It is the glory of God to conceal a thing: but the honour of kings is to search out a matter.\" (Proverbs 25:2) He conceals on purpose; searching it out is kingly honour. \"Then saith he unto his disciples, The harvest truly is plenteous, but the labourers are few;\" (Matthew 9:37) Production multiplied and the proving did not - and His answer was to ask for labourers, not for a larger harvest. \"But where shall wisdom be found? and where is the place of understanding?\" (Job 28:12) The chapter that admires every feat of engineering and then asks the one question capability never answers."
