      howToRun: "Prayer + the anchor (5): open in prayer; read Proverbs 11:1 and Ecclesiastes 10:10 aloud from the King James text. | Recap (8): what did you move out of an expensive path last week, and what did it cost before and after? | The two columns (12): draw SETTLED and JUDGMENT on a board and sort one real process the room shares; let the disagreements run, because the sorting is the skill. | The Word on weights (15): read Proverbs 11:1, 16:11, 20:10 and Leviticus 19:35-36 and name the register the text uses, then say plainly what that reframes. | Matthew 6:7, handled (8): read it, say it is about prayer, and teach the belief He corrected without stretching Him into engineering. | The blunt iron (7): read Ecclesiastes 10:10 and let the room tell their own version of putting to more strength. | Judgment is the work (10): Solomon's request and Hebrews 5:14, then Proverbs 18:13 on hearing before answering. | Plain enough to run with (5): Habakkuk 2:2 and Proverbs 27:23, and one honest gap each. | Close (5): two or three witnesses, Job 28:12, Psalms 127:1, and the week's one move named out loud by each person.",
