      "Counting placed where Scripture places it — before building, and sitting down (\"For which of you, intending to build a tower, sitteth not down first, and counteth the cost, whether he have sufficient to finish it?\" (Luke 14:28)) — with the mockery in the parable aimed at the unfinished, never the unattempted.",
      "Building named as three Resources rather than one: Wisdom builds, Understanding establishes, Knowledge fills (\"Through wisdom is an house builded; and by understanding it is established:\" (Proverbs 24:3)), itemised by name when Yahweh filled Bezaleel (\"And I have filled him with the spirit of God, in wisdom, and in understanding, and in knowledge, and in all manner of workmanship,\" (Exodus 31:3)), with Love senior to them all (\"And though I have the gift of prophecy, and understand all mysteries, and all knowledge; and though I have all faith, so that I could remove mountains, and have not charity, I am nothing.\" (1 Corinthians 13:2)).",
      "Ownership defined as answerability rather than possession (\"And he called him, and said unto him, How is it that I hear this of thee? give an account of thy stewardship; for thou mayest be no longer steward.\" (Luke 16:2)), so “who answers when this is asked about” becomes a question you can actually put to a system.",
