    "bigIdea": "THE LEADERS USE IT MORE THAN THE LED — PRETENDING TO KNOW IS A DEBT, AND NO WORKER IS UNTRACEABLE. Darrell forwarded a trade-association news digest on October 15, 2026 with one word on it: Lesson. The source is an advertising-dense daily email whose every news item is a second-hand summary of somebody else's reporting, with its own date and a link out, so the headline number is a claim by two named research firms, reported at three removes, and we say so rather than launder it into fact. The claim: 53.2 percent of executives use generative A.I. and only 37.9 percent of employees do; 18 percent of senior leaders pretend to understand more about it than they do; 27 percent would change jobs for better training. The Word has settled every piece of that and it is not a debate. A leader performing knowledge he does not have is already caught — \"For if a man think himself to be something, when he is nothing, he deceiveth himself.\" (Galatians 6:3) — and his gap is not a private embarrassment but a debt, because \"For unto whomsoever much is given, of him shall be much required: and to whom men have committed much, of him they will ask the more.\" (Luke 12:48) A shepherd is required to measure his own house — \"Be thou diligent to know the state of thy flocks, and look well to thy herds.\" (Proverbs 27:23) — and the gift came with an order to hand it on: \"And he hath put in his heart that he may teach\" (Exodus 35:34). Then the strangest item in the issue: an agent leaves no trace, so nobody can say who owns what it made. The Kingdom has no untraceable workers. \"give an account of thy stewardship\" (Luke 16:2), and Yahweh's own building projects print the builder's name.",
