      "theme": "A leader who performs knowledge he does not have is already judged by the Word, and the judgement is mercy, because the cure is instruction and the only person instruction cannot help is the one who hates reproof. The gap between a leader and the people he leads is a debt he owes them, not a secret he keeps: much given means much required, the blind cannot lead the blind, and the shepherd is commanded to know the state of his own flock by measurement rather than by feel. The same Word settles the newer question too. A worker who leaves no trace is a governance failure and not a feature, because every steward gives an account, the books are opened, and Yahweh's own building projects call the builder by name. And the skill the industry has just discovered — direct the machine, then evaluate what it made — is the believer's ordinary discipline with a salary attached: prove all things, try the spirits, search it out daily to see whether those things are so."
