      "research": "Do the count the survey cannot do for you, because it is about your house and not a sample of strangers. List every person on your team or in your family who could use the A.I. tools you have. Mark each one: uses it weekly, has tried it once, has never touched it. Then mark yourself honestly on the same list. Write the date at the top. Do not estimate and do not round; a counted number and a felt number are different things, and only one of them can be checked later.",
      "plan": "Now read your own sheet and name the gap out loud. If you are further along than the people you lead, that distance is the debt, and the plan is the repayment schedule: who gets taught, what one thing they get taught first, and on what day. Pick the smallest real lesson, not a programme — one tool, one task they already do, thirty minutes. If you are the one who has been nodding along in meetings, write down the one question you have been afraid to ask, and decide who you will ask it of this week.",
