      "theme": "KJV: \"Casting down imaginations, and every high thing that exalteth itself against the knowledge of God, and bringing into captivity every thought to the obedience of Christ;\" (2 Corinthians 10:5) - the mind is kept by taking thoughts captive, not by holding every thought at once, which is the whole of this week in one verse. And \"Then ye shall answer them, That the waters of Jordan were cut off before the ark of the covenant of the LORD; when it passed over Jordan, the waters of Jordan were cut off: and these stones shall be for a memorial unto the children of Israel for ever.\" (Joshua 4:7) - the river crossing went into storage and a sign stayed behind, which is the memory pointer three thousand years early. The spine runs from the sound mind and the kept heart (2 Timothy 1:7; Proverbs 4:23; Philippians 4:8; Isaiah 26:3), through the silent failure that throws no error (Proverbs 14:12; Revelation 3:17; Psalms 19:12), the increase that does not help (Ecclesiastes 1:18; Ecclesiastes 12:12; Proverbs 10:19; Matthew 6:7), the memorial that holds the pile outside while the sign stays in view (Joshua 4:6-7; Exodus 17:14; Malachi 3:16; Psalms 119:11; Deuteronomy 6:8-9), the cheap window that forgets what it learned (Psalms 78:11; Psalms 106:13; Deuteronomy 8:11; 2 Peter 1:9; Deuteronomy 4:9), the finished work that ends the labour and the folly that returns to it (John 19:30; Genesis 2:2; Hebrews 4:10; Philippians 1:6; Proverbs 26:11), the price that buys bulk and never buys truth (Proverbs 23:23; Acts 8:20; 1 Peter 1:18-19; Proverbs 17:16; Matthew 16:26), the words taken from a neighbour and the just weight (Jeremiah 23:30; Proverbs 22:28; Proverbs 11:1), the tower whose cost was not counted and the house on sand (Luke 14:28-30; Matthew 7:24-27; Genesis 11:4; Psalms 127:1), and the close where the Resources build the house and the words of the mouth are weighed (Proverbs 24:3-4; 1 Corinthians 13:1; Psalms 19:14)."
