      "howToRun": "Prayer + the anchor (5): open in prayer; read Hebrews 5:14 and Luke 2:52 aloud (KJV). | Recap last week (8): the pile, the pointer, and the clear done. | The source and our distance (7): name the digest, the outlets, Darrell's one word, and say out loud that we read no full article and reproduced no figure. | The Word on forming (10): Hebrews 5:12-14, Isaiah 28:10, Proverbs 22:6, Luke 6:40 - forming is bought with use. | The counting and the counter-witness (12): Luke 14:28-30 beside Daniel 1:4-20, so the room holds both without picking a camp. | Work beside learning (8): Berea, Paul's tents, Bezaleel's bench and his teaching commission. | Debt, wages, margins, weights (10): Proverbs 22:7 and Deuteronomy 15:1-2; the reported figures with the limit named; Leviticus 19:9-10; Proverbs 11:1. | The stranger (5): state the facts, refuse the party frame, teach Leviticus 19:34 and name the Word's silence on visa law. | Hands-on in the app (7): open a Living Lesson, use Search it out to fetch a verse live from our own corpus, then read the same lesson at the child band and at the adult band and see the ladder; then open Admin -> Systems and read Loop Health so the room sees live numbers rather than a painted one. | Close and send (3): Hall's three questions as the Word's test, then the talk-together assignment in all three directions.",
