          "explain": "The Lord Jesus said the labourer is worthy of his hire, \"And in the same house remain, eating and drinking such things as they give: for the labourer is worthy of his hire. Go not from house to house.\" (Luke 10:7) and Paul quotes Him as Scripture: \"For the scripture saith, Thou shalt not muzzle the ox that treadeth out the corn. And, The labourer is worthy of his reward.\" (1 Timothy 5:18) A reader who uses 2 Thessalonians 3:10 to shame the weak has run step five before step two. The Word is not against a paid teacher; it is for a formed one."
