        "Spend real time on the two speeds in Proverbs 24:34. Poverty comes \"as one that travelleth\" — walking toward you the whole time, closing distance while you sleep. Want comes \"as an armed man\" — all at once, in the doorway, with no negotiation. Then say the thing that makes it land: the decay and the incident are the same event seen at two distances, which is why the day everything fails feels like it came from nowhere.",
        "Name the trap in the article plainly, and do not soften it. If an outage is what finally gets the budget approved, then the outage is working for you, and a man can quietly make peace with a thing that keeps paying him. That is a toll, not prevention. Luke 12:39 puts the remedy in watching, not in funding afterwards.",
